% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/plan_notes.py` as the TRACK-scoped note override layer at plans/<slug>/notes.json. The global tracks.dj_notes column stays the default and plans store sparse overrides on top: this is the only design that gets per-plan divergence without orphaning hand-verified notes, which the sibling portable-collection intent requires outright, and the library index has no migration framework or version table so altering the column has no supported path anyway. get_effective(slug, track_ids) returns EffectiveNote with layer='plan'|'global' and a diverged flag. set_override/clear_override NEVER write tracks.dj_notes by any path; clearing falls back to the global note, never to ''. An override whose track is available=0 is RETAINED and flagged, never dropped, because an unmounted collection must not be read as deleted. Each accepted set/clear appends exactly one journal entry carrying the author already in its signature. Transition-scoped notes are module 10's, not this module's.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

TRACK-scoped note override layer at plans/<slug>/notes.json. The global tracks.dj_notes column stays the default and plans store sparse overrides on top: this is the only design that gets per-plan divergence without orphaning hand-verified notes, which the sibling portable-collection intent requires outright, and the library index has no migration framework or version table so altering the column has no supported path anyway. get_effective(slug, track_ids) returns EffectiveNote with layer='plan'|'global' and a diverged flag. set_override/clear_override NEVER write tracks.dj_notes by any path; clearing falls back to the global note, never to ''. An override whose track is available=0 is RETAINED and flagged, never dropped, because an unmounted collection must not be read as deleted. Each accepted set/clear appends exactly one journal entry carrying the author already in its signature. Transition-scoped notes are module 10's, not this module's.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/plan_notes.py`.
- PDD context tags: backend, plan, notes.
- Keep changes scoped to the primary output and the smallest necessary caller/test adaptations.

